{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks","id":696268,"title":"Questions about Malfeas and Ranks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-10T11:13:54-07:00","id":696268,"title":"Questions about Malfeas and Ranks","content":"one: How does malfeas exactly looks like? is there any art on its geography and such?<br /> two: is there any book where i can learn more about it?<br /> three: can normal humans (like pentex security) go there?<br /> Four: According to you, who outranks who. the fomor or the black spiral dancer<br /> <br /> And as for ranks: what if a rank 1 tries to use an fetishe of a higher rank? will the artifact stop working or ?<br /> <br /> and refresh my memory but. can garous harm spirits ? or do they need a gifts to do so?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":1754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","user":"Crowley","date":". 10-10-2015, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-10T11:20:15-07:00","id":696296,"title":"","content":"1 &amp;2 can be found into the W20 Book of the Wyrm, there are description of different wyrm creature territories laid out through out Malfeas. W20 Umbra also has some information on Malfeas as well.<br /> <br /> 3, They can be brought there but they can not get there on their own. Pentex, is more the pawn of a powerful spirit of the Wyrm whom they serve. They do not serve the wyrm directly like the BSD.<br /> <br /> 4, Black Spiral Dancers are the Alpha's in the Wyrms Service for now. The Yeren are a close second. Fomori are expendable cannon fodder.<br /> <br /> Rank has nothing do do with ones ability to use a fetish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T11:04:01-07:00","id":697575,"title":"","content":"What if the fomor is the vessel of a powerful bane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T11:59:29-07:00","id":697645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=697575#post697575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the fomor is the vessel of a powerful bane?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fomor would be still be seen as the bane's toy, and there would likely still be an expectation that the bane is going to shed the body at some point, so no serious harm done if the body gets killed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T11:59:51-07:00","id":697650,"title":"","content":"then it Creates a MIGHTY Formori<br /> <br /> Might be best if you have Demon the fallen or &quot;Devils due&quot; to use one of those books rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T12:43:21-07:00","id":697775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=697650#post697650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then it Creates a MIGHTY Formori</div> </div> </div> </div>Strictly speaking, there are hard limits on that. Pushing too hard destroys the human vessel, and what powers they do have tends to depend on how much of themselves the fomori have given up. (You give up Autonomy or take on negative traits to get powers, usually.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Might be best if you have Demon the fallen or &quot;Devils due&quot; to use one of those books rules. </div> </div> </div>Fomori are emphatically not like that, as explicitly noted in their entry of Possessed. Demon is where you go to have stories of redemption; playing a fomor is where you go to have an expected story of an internal death spiral that's much faster and more painful/Cronenbergian than in Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T16:03:12-07:00","id":698036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=697645#post697645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The fomor would be still be seen as the bane's toy, and there would likely still be an expectation that the bane is going to shed the body at some point, so no serious harm done if the body gets killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps, but since reading the section about familiars I am inclined to believe that spirits grow fastest when they have somehow become living, material brings. If the BSDs kill a strong Bane's unusually gifted xp machine, there might be some trouble. The smart ones probably make a note of which human is which Bane's mount.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T17:02:27-07:00","id":698120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=697775#post697775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fomori are emphatically not like that, as explicitly noted in their entry of Possessed. Demon is where you go to have stories of redemption; playing a fomor is where you go to have an expected story of an internal death spiral that's much faster and more painful/Cronenbergian than in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, with the right friends there might be help. I am reminded of a few aspects of the WoD, where in Hunter you can have sex with someone and use that as a means to sell their soul, since you are &quot;one flesh&quot; with that person. Or where if you sell your soul, you also sell out your Avatar. If a fomori can find the right person, they might have &quot;power of attorney&quot; over the bane's loyalty and state of being. Granted we are talking heavy duty magick/rites, but it's possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T07:12:14-07:00","id":702051,"title":"","content":"Crossing Mage with Werewolf is never a good idea. BSD should be the biggest and baddest does of the Garou. In chronicles where they are not used the Yeren make excellent substitutes. You don't want to use Yeren then go with the Vorstag. Formori are a tragedy most with few exceptions, Hollow Ones spring to mind, are cannon fodder not masterminds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T05:43:01-07:00","id":703241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=702051#post702051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Crossing Mage with Werewolf is never a good idea. BSD should be the biggest and baddest does of the Garou. In chronicles where they are not used the Yeren make excellent substitutes. You don't want to use Yeren then go with the Vorstag. Formori are a tragedy most with few exceptions, Hollow Ones spring to mind, are cannon fodder not masterminds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ok, thats a new one... Whats a Vorstag?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T07:02:23-07:00","id":703372,"title":"","content":"Apocalypse the final book introduced a new Wyrm creature that may or may not have ties to the Fianna's mythical foes. Most common in Northern climates and thought to have been exterminated. This is the Vorstag, note I am probably misspelling it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T09:11:46-07:00","id":703540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=703372#post703372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apocalypse the final book introduced a new Wyrm creature that may or may not have ties to the Fianna's mythical foes. Most common in Northern climates and thought to have been exterminated. This is the Vorstag, note I am probably misspelling it</div> </div> </div> </div>Vo'lag, the lost Giants. They're implied to be the Fomorians that the Tuatha fought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-16T19:46:34-07:00","id":704188,"title":"","content":"Thank you. I knew I had the name wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T01:23:08-07:00","id":704477,"title":"","content":"Could someone give a little more detail about the Vo'lag, they sound interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T01:36:50-07:00","id":704480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=704477#post704477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone give a little more detail about the Vo'lag, they sound interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's all in the apocalypse book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T02:58:20-07:00","id":704584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=704477#post704477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could someone give a little more detail about the Vo'lag, they sound interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Legendary Wyrmish Giants that live under the Earth and that come out to play with the Apocalypse. They are intended to represent legendary monsters of multiple mythologies. There is not much more on them, but take a look at the book, they are quite useable. I've actually ran a Irish game where the pack had to prevent Balor from freeing them from Earth and kickstarting the apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T08:37:21-07:00","id":705155,"title":"","content":"I also have used them. The chronicle was called Echoes of the Past. The Vo'lag fit better for the mood and theme of the story than a hive of BSD. I did add to them and gave them auspices, and BSD gifts. I was disappointed that they didn't make an appearance in the Book of the Wyrm 20.<br /> <br /> If I run a fall of the White Howlers I think the Vo'lag would be prime candidates for the Wyrm legion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-17T09:45:54-07:00","id":705252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/696268-questions-about-malfeas-and-ranks?p=702051#post702051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>BSD should be the biggest and baddest foes of the Garou.</b> In chronicles where they are not used the Yeren make excellent substitutes. You don't want to use Yeren then go with the Vorstag. Formori are a tragedy most with few exceptions, Hollow Ones spring to mind, are cannon fodder not masterminds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. BSDs are certainly the ones who can go toe-to-toe with Garou most easily, but their threat is mostly a very physical and spiritual one. They're not the ones responsible for Humanity falling to the Wyrm and dragging Gaia with it - Pentex is far better at that. They're also not the best at environmental destruction, they just don't have the numbers for it. All in all, they're a very serious threat, but I don't think they are <i>the</i> undisputed number one threat.<br /> And the Yeren are IMO definitely not ranking on any global threat scale yet. Their project is just past infancy and according to BotW20, there is no Yeren past rank 3. As the chapter describes, they have a very specific use: Targeting Bone Gnawer and Glass Walker bastions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> To answer the original questions:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> one: How does malfeas exactly looks like? is there any art on its geography and such?<br /> two: is there any book where i can learn more about it?<br /> three: can normal humans (like pentex security) go there?<br /> Four: According to you, who outranks who. the fomor or the black spiral dancer<br /> <br /> [Five] And as for ranks: what if a rank 1 tries to use an fetishe of a higher rank? will the artifact stop working or ?<br /> <br /> [Six] and refresh my memory but. can garous harm spirits ? or do they need a gifts to do so? </div> </div> </div>1+2) The Book of the Wyrm explains some of it. Basically, it's segregated into several duchies, with the central one being the domain of Number 2, the highest-ranking Black Spiral. The other duchies, belonging to the Urge Wyrms and their Maeljin Incarna are arranged like a wheel around it. While it isn't spelled out anywhere, I prefer to insert some amounts of non-euclidian geometry, and possibly suggest that the whole thing is built onto the pattern web holding the Wyrm captive, with its throes occassionally rippling through the realm.<br /> <br /> 3) Generally, they can't, unless they have some help from spirits or BSDs. However, humans can't live in the Umbra for a longer period of time, so most prefer to summon wyrmish spirits into the Tellurian rather than dealing with them on their home plane.<br /> <br /> 4) In general, Fomori are foot soldiers and cannon fodder. That being said, there are a few exceptions.<br /> <br /> 5) If you've got a fetish and manage the gnosis roll to switch it on, it works for you. However, a rank one Garou with a powerful fetish has a high chance of being challenged for it by a higher-ranking one.<br /> <br /> 6) Yes, Garou can harm spirits (as long as they're both in the Umbra or both in the Tellurian).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3118-cifer","name":"Cifer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3118_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1174"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}